  "details": "People go AFK in VRChat pretty often - it's a fairly normal occurrence. However, sometimes people go AFK in really inconvenient locations, such as:\n\n- In club worlds, people go AFK right in front of the DJ, blocking views\n\n- In video worlds, people go AFK in front of the screen, again blocking views\n\n- In game worlds, people go AFK in the waiting area, meaning they keep getting pulled into rounds while AFK\n\nAnd so on. This can range from a minor inconvenience to a disruption (imagine playing Among Us and an impostor is AFK).\n\nKicking someone for being AFK seems harsh, as does blocking them. So as an alternative, I propose adding an option for instance moderators to just respawn someone, so they can rejoin as soon as they're back, but they can be moved out of the way while they're not there.",
